# OpenSPP View Customization Best Practices

## Context
- When extending OpenSPP UI views (forms, trees, kanban, etc.)
- When adding custom fields to OpenSPP interfaces
- When modifying existing OpenSPP views
- When developing custom UI components for OpenSPP

## Requirements
- Extend existing views rather than replacing them
- Follow OpenSPP's view extension patterns
- Use proper view inheritance mechanisms
- Maintain consistent UI/UX with the core OpenSPP system
- Apply proper XML formatting and structure

## Key OpenSPP Views to Extend

### Individual Views
- **Tree View**: `g2p_registry_individual.view_individuals_list_tree`
- **Form View**: `g2p_registry_individual.view_individuals_form`

### Group Views
- **Tree View**: `g2p_registry_group.view_groups_list_tree`
- **Form View**: `g2p_registry_group.view_groups_form`

## Examples
<example>
<!-- Proper extension of Individual Form View -->
<odoo>
    <record id="view_individuals_form_custom" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">view_individuals_form_custom</field>
        <field name="model">res.partner</field>
        <field name="inherit_id" ref="g2p_registry_individual.view_individuals_form" />
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <xpath expr="//page[@name='basic_info']/group/group[1]" position="after">
                <group colspan="2">
                    <field name="z_cst_indv_disability_level"/>
                    <field name="z_cst_indv_education_level"/>
                </group>
            </xpath>
        </field>
    </record>
</odoo>
</example>

<example type="invalid">
<!-- Incorrect view extension with poor practices -->
<odoo>
    <record id="custom_individuals_form" model="ir.ui.view">
        <!-- Missing proper naming convention -->
        <field name="name">custom.form</field>
        <field name="model">res.partner</field>
        <!-- Missing inherit_id field to extend existing view -->
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <form>
                <!-- Replacing entire form instead of extending -->
                <sheet>
                    <group>
                        <field name="name"/>
                        <field name="disability_level"/>
                    </group>
                </sheet>
            </form>
        </field>
    </record>
</odoo>
</example>

## View Extension Guidelines

### XPath Usage
- Use XPath expressions to locate and modify specific parts of parent views
- Common position attributes:
  - `after`: Adds content after targeted element
  - `before`: Adds content before targeted element
  - `inside`: Adds content inside targeted element
  - `replace`: Replaces targeted element
  - `attributes`: Modifies attributes of targeted element

### Visibility Control
- Use `invisible` attribute to hide fields while keeping them in the view
- Example: `<field name="address" position="attributes"><attribute name="invisible">1</attribute></field>`

### Field Grouping
- Group related fields together for better UX
- Use `<group>` elements with proper `colspan` attributes

## Complete Examples

### Adding Custom Fields to Individual Tree View
```xml
<odoo>
    <record id="view_individuals_list_tree_custom" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">view_individuals_list_tree_custom</field>
        <field name="model">res.partner</field>
        <field name="inherit_id" ref="g2p_registry_individual.view_individuals_list_tree" />
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <xpath expr="//field[@name='address']" position="attributes">
                <attribute name="invisible">1</attribute>
            </xpath>
            <xpath expr="//field[@name='address']" position="after">
                <field name="z_cst_indv_disability_level" string="Disability Level" />
                <field name="z_cst_indv_education_level" string="Education" />
            </xpath>
        </field>
    </record>
</odoo>
```

### Adding Custom Fields to Group Form View
```xml
<odoo>
    <record id="view_groups_form_custom" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">view_groups_form_custom</field>
        <field name="model">res.partner</field>
        <field name="inherit_id" ref="g2p_registry_group.view_groups_form" />
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <xpath expr="//page[@name='basic_info']/group/group[1]" position="after">
                <group colspan="2">
                    <field name="z_ind_grp_num_children"/>
                    <field name="z_ind_grp_is_single_head_hh"/>
                    <field name="z_cst_grp_poverty_level"/>
                </group>
            </xpath>
        </field>
    </record>
</odoo>
```

## XML Formatting Best Practices
- Use 4 spaces for indentation
- Keep line length reasonable (120 characters max)
- Use consistent naming for view IDs
- Add comments for complex XPath expressions
- Group related view modifications together
- Use descriptive field labels with the `string` attribute
